# Android.
#
# android/ is generated — `npx cap add android` writes it from the Capacitor template and
# Dockerfile.android regenerates it on every build. Committing it would mean reviewing a
# few thousand lines of template on every Capacitor bump and would make the container build
# depend on a developer's local state. Native changes that must persist belong in
# android-config/, which is committed and overlaid after generation.
/android/
/dist-android/
/.gradle/
*.keystore
*.jks
local.properties
